{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3f1a2c8e-9b4d-4e2f-8a6b-7c5d0e1f2a3b",
    "name": "Facebook & TikTok Scraper - API complete + Ops",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Collection consolidee pour l'architecture RabbitMQ/MongoDB/Spring Boot + workers Python (Facebook, TikTok).\n\nOrganisation en 5 dossiers:\n1. Health & Infra (gateway + proxy IPv6 de rotation, legacy)\n2. Jobs - Creation (POST /scrape, csv-report, csv-report-24h)\n3. Jobs - Statut & Resultats (GET status/results/stream)\n4. Requetes DB (jobs/results avec filtres)\n5. Cas d'erreur (validation, 404)\n\nSTRATEGIE ANTI-DETECTION ACTUELLE: un batch CSV (csv-report / csv-report-24h)\nrepartit automatiquement ses pages sur les proxies definis dans\nTIKTOK_PROXY_LIST (.env, ex: 10 proxies Webshare), une lane parallele dediee\npar proxy (voir worker.py: get_proxy_pool / _split_round_robin). Rien a\nappeler manuellement pour ca, c'est automatique a chaque batch.\n\nNOTE sur le dossier 'Health & Infra > Proxy IPv6' (LEGACY, desactive par\ndefaut, TIKTOK_PROXY_SERVER vide dans .env): ancienne strategie de rotation\nbasee sur un bloc IPv6 /64 route sur le VPS (tools/ipv6_rotating_proxy.py),\nconservee pour reference/reactivation future. Ce proxy n'ecoute que sur\n127.0.0.1 du VPS, pour des raisons de securite (aucune authentification sur\n/rotate). Si vous l'utilisez et executez Postman depuis votre PC et non\ndepuis le VPS, il faut d'abord ouvrir un tunnel SSH:\n  ssh -L 8091:127.0.0.1:8091 -L 1080:127.0.0.1:1080 votre_user@votre_vps\nUne fois le tunnel ouvert, http://127.0.0.1:8091/... depuis Postman sur votre\nPC atteint bien le proxy du VPS.",
    "schema_note": "Toutes les reponses JSON de la gateway sont en snake_case (spring.jackson.property-naming-strategy=SNAKE_CASE)."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health & Infra",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Gateway Health - GET /actuator/health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/actuator/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verifie que la gateway Spring Boot est UP (et donc que sa connexion a MongoDB/RabbitMQ fonctionne)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Status is UP', function () {",
                  "    const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(data.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Proxy IPv6 (legacy) - Status - GET /status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{proxy_control_base_url}}/status",
              "host": [
                "{{proxy_control_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "status"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verifie que le proxy SOCKS5 de rotation IPv6 (systemd, sur le VPS) est bien demarre. Necessite un tunnel SSH si Postman tourne hors du VPS (voir description de la collection)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Body starts with OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('OK');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Proxy IPv6 (legacy) - Forcer une rotation - GET /rotate",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{proxy_control_base_url}}/rotate",
              "host": [
                "{{proxy_control_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rotate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Force le proxy a choisir immediatement une nouvelle adresse IPv6 aleatoire dans le bloc /64 configure (IPV6_PROXY_PREFIX). C'est le meme endpoint que scraper.py appelle automatiquement toutes les TIKTOK_IPV6_ROTATE_EVERY_N_POSTS videos: utile ici pour tester manuellement la rotation sans lancer un scraping complet.\n\nAppelez deux fois de suite et comparez le corps de la reponse: l'adresse doit changer."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.text();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains new IPv6 address', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.match(/OK\\s+[0-9a-fA-F:]+/);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('Nouvelle adresse IPv6 du proxy:', body.trim());"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Jobs - Creation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Job Facebook - POST /scrape",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/some-page-or-post\",\n  \"platform\": \"facebook\",\n  \"max_posts\": 5\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cree un job de scraping Facebook et memorise scrape_id_facebook."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains scrape_id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.scrape_id).to.exist;",
                  "});",
                  "if (data.scrape_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id_facebook', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_facebook', '');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Job TikTok - POST /scrape",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://www.tiktok.com/@bellewarmedia\",\n  \"platform\": \"tiktok\",\n  \"max_posts\": 10\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Panel news Mauritanie (@bellewarmedia). Lancer aussi @kingmauritan / @tawaturnet separement — pas @tiktok."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains scrape_id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.scrape_id).to.exist;",
                  "});",
                  "if (data.scrape_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id_tiktok', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_tiktok', '');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create CSV Batch Report TikTok - POST /scrape/csv-report",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "{{csv_file_path}}",
                  "description": "Fichier CSV contenant des URLs de profils TikTok"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/csv-report",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "csv-report"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cree un job batch CSV TikTok (nombre fixe de posts par page) et retourne scrape_id + nombre d'URLs detectees."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains scrape_id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.scrape_id).to.exist;",
                  "});",
                  "if (data.scrape_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id_tiktok', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_tiktok', '');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create CSV Batch Report TikTok 24h - POST /scrape/csv-report-24h",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "{{csv_file_path}}",
                  "description": "Fichier CSV contenant des URLs de profils TikTok"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/csv-report-24h",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "csv-report-24h"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cree un job batch CSV TikTok avec fenetre automatique des dernieres 24h (pas de maxPostsPerPage: chaque page scrolle jusqu'a sortir de la fenetre de 24h). C'est ce endpoint qui beneficie le plus de la repartition en parallele sur TIKTOK_PROXY_LIST (une lane/proxy dediee par groupe de pages, voir worker.py)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains scrape_id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.scrape_id).to.exist;",
                  "});",
                  "if (data.scrape_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('scrape_id_tiktok', data.scrape_id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_tiktok', '');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Jobs - Statut & Resultats",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Job Status - GET /scrape/{scrapeId}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/{{scrape_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "{{scrape_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Statut du dernier job cree (QUEUED, RUNNING, SUCCESS, PARTIAL_SUCCESS ou FAILED). PARTIAL_SUCCESS signifie que des posts ont ete recuperes malgre une erreur/challenge en cours de route (voir metadata pour le detail)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (data.metadata && data.metadata.jsonPath) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('batch_report_json_path', data.metadata.jsonPath);",
                  "}",
                  "console.log('Job status:', data.status);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Job Results (snapshot complet) - GET /scrape/{scrapeId}/results",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/{{scrape_id}}/results",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "{{scrape_id}}",
                "results"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Recupere TOUS les resultats stockes en MongoDB pour ce scrape_id (snapshot, pas de pagination)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200 or 202', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 202]);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has results array', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.results).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Stream Results Facebook (cursor + long-poll) - GET /scrape/{scrapeId}/results/stream",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/{{scrape_id_facebook}}/results/stream?cursor={{result_cursor_facebook}}&limit=5&waitMs=15000",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "{{scrape_id_facebook}}",
                "results",
                "stream"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "cursor",
                  "value": "{{result_cursor_facebook}}",
                  "description": "Cursor renvoye par l'appel precedent (vide au premier appel)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "waitMs",
                  "value": "15000",
                  "description": "Long-poll en ms (0..30000)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Ne retourne que les NOUVEAUX resultats apres le cursor (mode progressif). Rejouez cette requete en boucle jusqu'a done=true. Met a jour result_cursor_facebook automatiquement."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (data.next_cursor !== undefined) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_facebook', data.next_cursor || '');",
                  "}",
                  "console.log('done=', data.done, 'status=', data.status, 'count=', data.count);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Stream Results TikTok (cursor + long-poll) - GET /scrape/{scrapeId}/results/stream",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/{{scrape_id_tiktok}}/results/stream?cursor={{result_cursor_tiktok}}&limit=5&waitMs=15000",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "{{scrape_id_tiktok}}",
                "results",
                "stream"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "cursor",
                  "value": "{{result_cursor_tiktok}}",
                  "description": "Cursor renvoye par l'appel precedent (vide au premier appel)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "waitMs",
                  "value": "15000",
                  "description": "Long-poll en ms (0..30000)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Ne retourne que les NOUVEAUX resultats apres le cursor (mode progressif). Rejouez cette requete en boucle jusqu'a done=true. Met a jour result_cursor_tiktok automatiquement."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (data.next_cursor !== undefined) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('result_cursor_tiktok', data.next_cursor || '');",
                  "}",
                  "console.log('done=', data.done, 'status=', data.status, 'count=', data.count);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Requetes DB (jobs/resultats avec filtres)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List Jobs DB - GET /scrape/jobs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/jobs?platform=tiktok&status=SUCCESS&limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "jobs"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "platform",
                  "value": "tiktok",
                  "description": "facebook|tiktok (optionnel)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "SUCCESS",
                  "description": "QUEUED|RUNNING|SUCCESS|PARTIAL_SUCCESS|FAILED (optionnel)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liste les jobs stockes en MongoDB avec filtres optionnels."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has jobs array', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.jobs).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List Results DB - GET /scrape/results",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/results?scrapeId={{scrape_id}}&platform=tiktok&limit=100",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "results"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "scrapeId",
                  "value": "{{scrape_id}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "platform",
                  "value": "tiktok",
                  "description": "facebook|tiktok (optionnel)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liste les resultats stockes en MongoDB avec filtres optionnels."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has results array', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(data.results).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Cas d'erreur",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validation Error - POST /scrape (plateforme invalide)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com\",\n  \"platform\": \"instagram\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Teste l'erreur metier pour une plateforme non supportee (doit repondre 400)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Not Found - GET /scrape/{scrapeId inexistant}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scrape/not-existing-id",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape",
                "not-existing-id"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Teste le 404 quand le scrape_id n'existe pas."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 404', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
